<style>
    body {
        margin: 0;
        background-color: #3f4632;
        font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    }

    .faq-wrapper {
        padding: 60px;
    }

    .faq-grid {
        display: flex;
        flex-wrap: wrap;
        gap: 30px;
    }

    .faq-card {
        flex: 1 1 calc(33.333% - 30px);
        min-width: 280px;
        box-sizing: border-box;
        border: 1px solid #fff;
        padding: 30px;
    }

        .faq-card h2 {
            color: #fff;
            font-size: 1.3rem;
            margin: 0 0 20px 0;
            line-height: 1.4;
        }

    .faq-divider {
        border: none;
        border-top: 1px solid #fff;
        width: 90%;
        margin: 0 0 20px 0;
    }

    .faq-card p {
        color: #fff;
        font-size: 1rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
        margin: 0;
    }
</style>

<div class="faq-wrapper">
    <div class="faq-grid">

        <div class="faq-card">
            <h2>What is Child and Youth Care?</h2>
            <hr class="faq-divider">
            <p>
                Child and Youth Care focuses on supporting the social, emotional,
                behavioural and developmental needs of children and young people.
                It involves working with young people in the context of their
                families, schools, communities and everyday lives to help them
                navigate challenges and reach their potential.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-card">
            <h2>What is LifeSpace Counselling?</h2>
            <hr class="faq-divider">
            <p>
                LifeSpace counselling is counselling that takes place within the
                young person's everyday environment and lived experience. Rather
                than only focusing on what happens during a counselling session,
                it considers the young person's relationships, family, school,
                community, emotions and circumstances.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-card">
            <h2>What is Resilience Building?</h2>
            <hr class="faq-divider">
            <p>
                Resilience building involves helping children, young people and
                families develop the skills, strengths and support systems they
                need to cope with challenges, recover from difficulties and adapt
                to change.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-card">
            <h2>What is Psychosocial Support?</h2>
            <hr class="faq-divider">
            <p>
                Psychosocial support addresses both a person's emotional and
                social wellbeing. It may include helping someone manage stress,
                cope with difficult experiences, strengthen relationships,
                develop coping skills and connect with appropriate support
                systems.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-card">
            <h2>What is Youth Development?</h2>
            <hr class="faq-divider">
            <p>
                Youth development is about helping young people develop the
                knowledge, skills, confidence and opportunities they need to
                become healthy, responsible and empowered individuals. This can
                include life skills, leadership, career guidance, decision-making,
                communication and personal development.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-card">
            <h2>What are Youth Mentorship Programmes?</h2>
            <hr class="faq-divider">
            <p>
                Mentorship programmes connect young people with a supportive
                adult or mentor who can provide guidance, encouragement,
                accountability and positive role modelling as they navigate
                personal, academic or career-related challenges.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-card">
            <h2>Who can benefit from Re-Center Hub's services?</h2>
            <hr class="faq-divider">
            <p>
                Our services can benefit children, adolescents, young adults,
                parents, caregivers, schools and community organisations seeking
                support with personal development, wellbeing, relationships,
                life skills and youth development.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-card">
            <h2>Do you only provide counselling?</h2>
            <hr class="faq-divider">
            <p>
                No. Re-Center Hub takes a holistic approach. Our services may
                include LifeSpace counselling and wellness support, life skills
                and education, youth development, mentorship and
                resilience-building initiatives.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-card">
            <h2>When should someone seek support?</h2>
            <hr class="faq-divider">
            <p>
                You don't have to wait until a problem becomes overwhelming.
                Support can be useful when someone is experiencing stress,
                relationship difficulties, major life changes, low confidence,
                academic challenges, behavioural concerns or simply feels unsure
                about how to move forward.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-card">
            <h2>Is counselling only for people experiencing serious problems?</h2>
            <hr class="faq-divider">
            <p>
                No. Counselling can also be used for personal growth,
                self-awareness, decision-making, emotional wellbeing and
                navigating everyday life challenges.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="faq-card">
            <h2>How does Re-Center Hub support young people?</h2>
            <hr class="faq-divider">
            <p>
                We focus on meeting young people where they are, understanding
                their individual circumstances and helping them develop
                strengths, coping skills, confidence and supportive relationships.
            </p>
        </div>

    </div>
</div>